commit 3d7693f793afd2c9de34cc93a1722984f90c81b5
Author: Sean Murphy <murphy@halfast.com>
Date:   Fri Aug 7 13:20:09 2026 -0700

    rocm: add real gfx12 (RDNA4) WMMA v2 matmul kernel for gfx1201

    Ports origin/gfx1201-discrete-gpu's d9be29f (from the ds4-rebase repo)
    onto this tree, replacing the DS4_ROCM_NO_WMMA opt-out fallback with a
    working matrix-core path for matmul_q8_0_f32_batch_wmma_4w_kernel.

    The literal d9be29f port (raw __builtin_amdgcn_wmma_..._gfx12 intrinsic,
    halved <8 x f16> fragments) was empirically wrong on real R9700 hardware:
    full-model logits and greedy generation diverged completely from the
    DS4_ROCM_NO_WMMA baseline. Three plausible fragment-layout fixes for the
    raw intrinsic all failed against a CPU reference in a standalone
    microbenchmark. Replaced with rocwmma::fragment-based load_matrix_sync/
    mma_sync/store_matrix_sync -- the same library API this file already
    uses correctly on gfx1201 for the MoE hotlist kernels -- which matches
    the CPU reference to fp16-rounding precision and reproduces the baseline's
    full-model argmax and greedy generation exactly.

    Adds a new `rdna4-wmma` build target; the existing `rdna4` default
    (DS4_ROCM_NO_WMMA) is unchanged pending wider validation, per this
    project's validate-before-default precedent.

    A/B via ds4-bench (single R9700, --ssd-streaming): prefill +14.5% at
    ctx=2048 (98.46->112.74 t/s avg of 2 runs), +1.9% at ctx=4096. Decode is
    flat by design -- this kernel only fires for n_tok>=256 batched prefill
    calls; decode's n_tok==1 path is untouched.

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

